#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087473 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37a4168b-1425-5f3a-a577-4b5884906a52" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Sum of a Complex Number and Its Conjugate"}] :question/id #uuid "ad30d35a-4fd5-593e-bb61-a3ac833668a5" :question/math-academy-id "e-5252" :question/problem "If $z=7-3\\textrm{i}$, calculate $z+\\overline{z}$." :question/worked-solution "*Method 1*\n\nWhen we add a complex number and its conjugate, the result is always twice the real part of the complex number.\n\nFor the given complex number\n\n$$\nz=7-3\\textrm{i}\n$$\n\nthe real part is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{Re}(z) = 7\n$$\n\nso we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nz + z^(―) &= 2Re(z) \\\\\n&= 2(7) \\\\\n&= 14\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Method 2*\n\nAlternatively, we can actually carry out the process of adding the complex number and its conjugate.\n\nTo obtain the conjugate of the complex number\n\n$$\nz=7-3\\textrm{i}\n$$\n\nwe flip the sign of the imaginary part and get\n\n$$\n\\overline{z} = 7 + 3 \\textrm{i}\n$$\n\nAdding, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nz + z^(―) &= (7 - 3\\textrm{i}) + (7 + 3\\textrm{i}) \\\\\n&= (7 + 7) + (-3\\textrm{i} + 3\\textrm{i}) \\\\\n&= 14 + \\textrm{i}0 \\\\\n&= 14\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087474 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "64cd3ef1-6d41-50c6-b09d-cb709d89281f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Product of a Complex Number and Its Conjugate"}] :question/id #uuid "135dcf7f-99e7-5ad0-b142-b9782fbc5fb3" :question/math-academy-id "e-5254" :question/problem "Given that $z=7-4\\textrm{i}$, calculate $z\\overline{z}$." :question/worked-solution "*Method 1*\n\nWhen we multiply a complex number and its conjugate, the result is always the sum of squares of the real part and the imaginary part.\n\nFor the given complex number\n\n$$\nz=7-4\\textrm{i}\n$$\n\nthe real part is\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Re}(z)=7\n$$\n\nand the imaginary part is\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Im}(z)=-4\n$$\n\nso we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nzz^(―) &= (Re(z))^{2} + (Im(z))^{2} \\\\\n&= 7^{2} + (-4)^{2} \\\\\n&= 49 + 16 \\\\\n&= 65\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Method 2*\n\nAlternatively, we can actually carry out the process of multiplying the complex number and its conjugate.\n\nTo obtain the conjugate of the complex number\n\n$$\nz=7-4\\textrm{i}\n$$\n\nwe flip the sign of the imaginary part and get\n\n$$\n\\overline{z} = 7 + 4 \\textrm{i}\n$$\n\nMultiplying, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nzz^(―) &= (7 - 4\\textrm{i})(7 + 4\\textrm{i}) \\\\\n&= 7^{2} + (7)(4)\\textrm{i} + (-4)(7)\\textrm{i} - (4)^{2}\\textrm{i}^{2} \\\\\n&= 49 + 28\\textrm{i} - 28\\textrm{i} - (16)(-1) \\\\\n&= 49 + 16 \\\\\n&= 65\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
